notes: |
  Three commits + 1 docs, found during iterative browser verification
  of mobile split-pane layout.

  1. **CSS comment bug** (335d312): stray `*/` without matching `/*`
     in components.css:2603. Vite minifier kept it in bundled output,
     browser parser treated ~60% of CSS as comment. .app-body
     `flex: 1 1 auto` was invisible. One-line fix.

  2. **Sheet ≥ 50vh** (335d312): peek/half 30/40→50vh, full stays
     65vh, default --sheet-h 40→50vh, min-height: 50vh on .wc-sheet
     (CSS hard floor). SHEET_HEIGHT_MIN_PX 240→360.

  3. **Remove .score-panel max-height** (b8e8193): The formula
     `calc(100dvh - 48 - 56 - 50vh)` was a "safety ceiling" but
     actually capped score-panel at ~346px on 900vh, leaving 374px
     of empty space. flex:1 + min-height:200 distributes correctly
     without the artificial ceiling. Result: sheet closed cm-host
     655px (50+ lines, was 281px before this fix).

  4. **Tab → sheet at half** (1d51ee6): setTab('piano'|'ai'|'mixer'|
     'step'|'status') was calling openKindSheet(kind, 'full') — sheet
     65vh, editor 105px. Changed all to 'half' — sheet 50vh,
     editor 240px (~18 lines). User can still drag to 'full' if
     they need more sheet space.

  Effect on 412×900 mobile:
  - sheet closed: cm-host 655px, 50+ lines visible.
  - sheet open half (50vh): cm-host 240px, ~18 lines.
  - sheet open full (65vh): cm-host 105px, ~8 lines.
  - drag-to-resize physically can't go below 50vh (CSS min-height).
  - tab → sheet opens at half by default.

  Verification:
  - tsc --noEmit: clean
  - vitest: 729/729 pass (no JS logic changes, CSS-only + 1 snap param)
  - vite build: success, 9s
  - production deploy via bin/deploy.sh: confirmed on
    https://wavecode.kosov.online — see browser screenshots.
